    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output #1

1.1.1. 11 new Youth Centers established in target locations with respective Youth Action Groups and Youth Action Plans 
1.1.2. 20 Youth Entrepreneurship Coordination Platforms established with 20 youth-friendly Local Investment Programmes  
1.1.3. 400 youth directly and 45,000 youth indirectly (50% young women) benefiting from the improved local mechanisms, tools and institutions
1.1.4. One analytical report with policy recommendations to sustain youth centers developed and submitted to the Government&#x2019;s consideration and follow up   
1.1.5. One online platform (website) developed and operational aimed at increasing coordination among key stakeholders  
1.2.1. Technical or vocational training provided for at least 100 youth, with at least 50% for young women
1.2.2. 50 students from Kyrgyzstan are prepared to participate in the international engineering championship 
1.2.3. At least 2 Russian expertise engaged from highly qualified green business mentors and private sector through the EAEU Secretariat
1.2.4. At least 1 strategic partnership is established between the Federal Agency on Youth Affairs of the Russian Federation and the Ministry of Culture and Youth of the Kyrgyz Republic

Output # 2

2.1.1. Business advisory support delivered to 400 direct youth beneficiaries (50% young women) 
2.1.2. At least 1 Russian expertise engaged from the municipalities of the Russian Federation that have vast experience in the development of youth entrepreneurship with a focus on green entrepreneurship  
2.2.1. At least 2 fund revolving schemes operationalized for sustainable funding of youth green entrepreneurship 
2.2.2. At least 100 new green businesses established, and employment provided for at least 300 youth (50% young women)
2.3.1. 20 youth-friendly Local Investments Programmes supported with small grants by the project 
2.3.2. Local governments allocated at least 30% of funds for implementing youth-friendly Local Investment Programmes from local budgets to im</narrative>
    </description>
